  "result": "Fixed, and all 8 tests now pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/pricing.py:10`, the bulk check was `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD`, so with the threshold at 10 the discount only started at 11 units. The policy is \"10 or more\", so it should have been `>=`.\n\n**Fix:** I changed it to `line.qty >= BULK_THRESHOLD`.\n\n**Tests:**\n- Before the fix, the existing `test_bulk_discount` test was already failing. For 10 units at $1.00 it got 1083 cents instead of 1028, which is the customer's bug exactly.\n- I added two more tests to `tests/test_pricing.py`:\n  - 9 units gets no discount (974 cents total).\n  - 10 units added in two batches (4 + 6) still gets the discount, because the cart combines them into one line.\n\nI haven't committed the changes.",
